  "post": {
    "caption": "Chanel's cuffs came from a Sicilian duke. Fulco di Verdura grew up in Palermo, Sicily, with a private zoo that included a camel. He spent most of his inheritance on one costume ball. Then Coco Chanel hired him in Paris, first for textiles, and soon for her jewelry. His Maltese cross cuff mixed white enamel with colorful stones, and Chanel wore the cuffs in a famous photograph. In 1939 he opened his own salon at 712 Fifth Avenue in New York, backed by Cole Porter. He even set real seashells in gold and gems.",
